Seal Eggs Redux Attribution – No Sale License 1.0
LicenseRef-Seal-Eggs-Redux-No-Sale-1.0
Copyright (c) 2026 vwal

1. Scope
These terms apply to original work for which vwal controls the rights in
Seal Eggs Redux, including the new firmware additions, patches, website,
reference publications and their copyrightable derivatives. Intellijel
firmware, BRIBERY's Seal Eggs, Mutable Instruments Beads, stmlib, webdfu
and other pre-existing material have their own owners and terms. This
license grants no rights in their firmware, code, trademarks or artwork.
All independent permissions and applicable third-party notices survive.

2. Grant and attribution
You may use, study, copy, adapt, merge, compile and share the covered
work without charge, subject to this license. Include vwal's copyright,
the complete license and applicable third-party notices with copies or
substantial portions. Mark your changes. For print, retain a readable
attribution and link to the full license. Free derivatives must preserve
these conditions on the covered portions. Use in paid performances,
studio work, lessons, and the sale or licensing of music and recordings
made with the module are permitted. The license does not attach to that
creative output through use of the tools.

3. No sale or paid supply
Except as permitted in section 4 or by separate written permission, you
may not supply the covered work or its derivatives for payment, whether
as a download, update, subscription, paid bundle, product, preinstalled
module or paid installation, build, modification or hosting service.
Describing an included component as a free bonus does not remove this
condition. Unconditional voluntary donations are permitted. Access and
delivery may not depend on a donation, membership or purchase.

4. Official Intellijel exception for the Redux firmware delta
This exception applies only to vwal's original firmware changes supplied
in the Redux delta over BRIBERY's Seal Eggs. BRIBERY separately licenses
its own Seal Eggs work under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
with express additional permissions for music and for Intellijel. The
scope of each grant is determined by its respective author. See
notices/Seal-Eggs-LICENSE.md for BRIBERY's complete terms. Third-party
terms also apply when their material is present in a combined image.

Intellijel, the manufacturer of Sealegs, may use, modify, incorporate,
reproduce, sublicense, distribute and sell those Redux changes in its
official products, firmware, updates and associated services without
further permission or a fee. This includes contractors and authorized
distributors acting on its behalf solely for that official integration
and distribution, and the subsequent resale of those official products.
Intellijel may license the resulting products under its own terms while
preserving the applicable copyright, attribution and license notices.
This exception overrides the no-sale conditions on vwal's work for those
uses only. It confers no right to sublicense BRIBERY's work or pass on
BRIBERY's separate Intellijel permission. Other rights holders' terms
still apply. No endorsement or obligation by Intellijel is implied.

5. Warranty and liability
The covered work is provided as is, without express or implied warranties,
including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and
noninfringement. To the extent permitted by applicable law, the authors
and rights holders shall not be liable for any claim, damage or liability
arising out of the work, its distribution or its use. Nothing in this
license limits rights that applicable law makes non-excludable.

This custom license applies only to Redux contributions. The MIT permissions
for Beads/stmlib and the Intellijel updater libraries and the ISC permissions
for webdfu remain in effect for their respective components. For upstream
credits and notices see THIRD-PARTY.md.

